        "original_id": "735e21c6-f46d-582e-b397-9b301bbd9e89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Green Bushes, Lincolnshire Posy, Lost Lady Found, The Cutty Wren\n- People: Percy Grainger\n- Organizations: American Bandmasters Association\n- Topics: melody similarity, composition\n\nFacts:\n- In 1937, Percy Grainger composed Lincolnshire Posy for concert band for the American Bandmasters Association.\n- The melody of Green Bushes is very similar to the melody of the \"Lost Lady Found\" movement in Percy Grainger's Lincolnshire Posy.\n- The melody of Green Bushes is also very similar to the melody of The Cutty Wren.",
